5e73a51187ac9b`; 1120-byte receipt hashes to `919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd`; both byte-match their goldens; marker equals `portable_identity.marker`; aliases is false; portable, legacy rc.4, and reserved-hardened keys are distinct and each re-derives from its own vector input with schema-valid flags true/false/false.'"\\n- The consumer architecture is independent: test support only resolves and verifies the caller root, reads authoritative JSON/bytes, invokes public "'`csk` boundaries, and compares outcomes. Framing, canonicalization, ordering, and protocol arithmetic are assigned to product modules, not copied into pytest helpers or derived from Curator Go source. Schema cases use product readers and manifest-covered cases rather than vendored schemas or a second oracle.'"\\n- Fixture strategy is complete and non-mutating: authoritative fixtures are copied to "'`tmp_path`, both manifest names are exercised independently, copy fidelity is checked, build/runtime/context boundaries are explicit, and Windows symlink/case behavior has qualification-vs-local policy. Current CocoaSkills is clean at `edce881`; the cited existing modules and CI pin exist, while proposed `src/csk/builds/*` and focused pytest modules are correctly identified as future owning-task surfaces.'"\\n- Drift is truthful. The attached released-pin log is 98 passed at rc.2 manifest "'`728f772950414b9c3ddf38a8f1e9f2c7d2953bdca1d8c135c7e1a9abf40fff06`; the candidate log is 1 failed / 97 passed at rc.5. The two shared fixture manifests are semantically identical after JSON normalization, and current `load_skill_spec` reads only `csk-skill.json`, so `agent-skill.json` produces an empty spec and incorrectly includes `scripts/golden-tool`. The design routes the exact AC correction to existing owner TASK-260720-z9j4c9 instead of inventing a duplicate task.'"\\n- Platform policy matches the accepted boundary: portable data on every platform; native host and real Go behavior