`529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b`; 1120-byte receipt hashes to `919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd`; both byte-match their goldens; marker equals `portable_identity.marker`; aliases is false; portable, legacy rc.4, and reserved-hardened keys are distinct and each re-derives from its own vector input with schema-valid flags true/false/false.'"\\n- The consumer architecture is independent: test support only resolves and verifies the caller root, reads authoritative JSON/bytes, invokes public "'`csk` boundaries, and compares outcomes. Framing, canonicalization, ordering, and protocol arithmetic are assigned to product modules, not copied into pytest helpers or derived from Curator Go source. Schema cases use product readers and manifest-covered cases rather than vendored schemas or a second oracle.'"\\n- Fixture strategy is complete and non-mutating: authoritative fixtures are copied to "'`tmp_path`, both manifest names are exercised independently, copy fidelity is checked, build/runtime/context boundaries are explicit, and Windows symlink/case behavior has qualification-vs-local policy. Current CocoaSkills is clean at `edce881`; the cited existing modules and CI pin exist, while proposed `src/csk/builds/*` and focused pytest modules are correctly identified as future owning-task surfaces.'"\\n- Drift is truthful. The attached released-pin log is 98 passed at rc.2 manifest "'`728f772950414b9c3ddf38a8f1e9f2c7d2953bdca1d8c135c7e1a9abf40fff06`; the candidate log is 1 failed / 97 passed at rc.5. The two shared fixture manifests are semantically identical after JSON normalization, and current `load_skill_spec` reads only `csk-skill.json`, so `agent-skill.json` produces an empty spec and incorrectly includes `scripts/golden-tool`. The design routes the exact AC correction to existing owner TASK-260720-z9j4c9 instead of inventing a duplicate task.'"\\n- Platform policy matches the accepted boundary: portable data on every platform; native host and real Go behavior on macOS/Windows; Linux driver success deferred, with Linux asserting fail-closed and no worker launch. Missing current-platform prerequisites fail in qualification jobs and may skip only in developer runs with explicit reasons; xfail is prohibited.\\n- Literal first-wave pytest commands, environment inputs, skip audit, typing gate, module ownership, and wave ordering are present. The proposed files do not yet exist by design; the statement that wave-1 feasibility passes is supported by the independently reproduced primitive/golden checks, while the literal pytest commands remain implementation gates for TASK-260720-12r55p after those test files are created.\\n\\n## Verdict\\nACCEPTED. The outcome maps every required rc.5 cluster to an independent Python consumer boundary and exact test surface, preserves the previous default pin, records digest provenance and truthful drift, covers positive/rejection/identity/lifecycle/platform/non-alias behavior, and supplies actionable first-wave pytest gates. No correction or external decision is required for this design task. Route to "'`done`." )'"'" in /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator
