- Inventory matches exactly: 8 positives, 77 rejections over 10 boundaries and 58 distinct error codes, 10 build-source cases, 12 toolchain cases, 5 argv forms, 28 fixed-environment keys; execution policy has 18 mandatory controls, 5 controls across exactly macOS and Windows, 14 identity/protocol, 8 package-influence, 11 capability-evidence, 8 consistency, 6 paired deferred guards, 3 failure boundaries, 13 session states, 4 process-graph nodes, and 6 policy semantics. The seven in-scope schema directories total 102 cases with the stated per-directory counts. Manager lifecycle and claim-v3 qualification are mapped to exact tests and product boundaries.
- Identity and non-alias evidence independently reproduces from authoritative JSON through CocoaSkills `csk.audit_registry.canonical_bytes`: 869-byte build input hashes to `529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b`; 1120-byte receipt hashes to `919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd`; both byte-match their goldens; marker equals `portable_identity.marker`; aliases is false; portable, legacy rc.4, and reserved-hardened keys are distinct and each re-derives from its own vector input with schema-valid flags true/false/false.
- The consumer architecture is independent: test support only resolves and verifies the caller root, reads authoritative JSON/bytes, invokes public `csk` boundaries, and compares outcomes. Framing, canonicalization, ordering, and protocol arithmetic are assigned to product modules, not copied into pytest helpers or derived from Curator Go source. Schema cases use product readers and manifest-covered cases rather than vendored schemas or a second oracle.
